  "category_mapping": "BUILTIN.DF(customer.category) on 2026-09-05: 2=Garage Experts (excluded), 3=DIY, 4=Contractor, 7=CA Will Call (retained), 14=Vendor (excluded).",
  "customers_with_no_state": 10,
  "definition": "customers: count of customer RECORDS with subsidiary=2, stage LIKE 'CUSTOMER%', firstorderdate IS NOT NULL, category NOT IN (2,14), and datecreated (cohort month) in 2025-09-01..2026-08-31, grouped by the 2-letter state of the customer's default shipping address (LEFT JOIN; customers with none are counted in customers_with_no_state). This is a record count, not the cohorts_m1 'customers' figure, which counts only customers with M1 revenue. m1_net_revenue: NET revenue (canonical join: CustInvc/CashSale/CustCred/CustRfnd, mainline='F', taxline='F', item NOT NULL, item.itemtype NOT NULL, SUM(-foreignamount)) from transactions whose trandate falls in the same calendar month as the customer's datecreated, summed over the 12 cohort months and grouped by the same state. m13_net_revenue_closed_cohorts_only: same NET join, trandate >= TRUNC(datecreated) AND trandate < TRUNC(datecreated) + 90 (first 90 calendar days starting on the creation DAY, identical to cohorts_m13.sql), summed over only the cohorts whose 90-day window is closed as of 2026-09-05 (month_end + 90 <= as_of): 2025-09..2026-05. Cohorts 2026-06..2026-08 contribute 0 to this column by construction. Each transaction-joined month was pulled as a separate SuiteQL call and summed in Python; per-cohort totals reconcile to the cent with cohorts_m1 (2025-09..2026-05, 2026-08) and cohorts_m13 (all 9 closed cohorts) snapshots. Sorted by customers desc.",
